  "slug": "current-cosmological-53cb",
  "summary": "New fits of axion and double-power scalar-field dark energy to DESI BAO, CMB and SN data coincide with BAO and low-z supernova probe developments.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is testing dark energy beyond a fixed positive cosmological constant with current distance and growth data. One analysis fits axion quintessence with a negative cosmological constant to DES, DESI BAO, CMB and growth data and finds no compelling evidence for a negative value. Another tests a single canonical scalar field with a double-power potential as unified early and late dark energy against CMB, DESI BAO and Pantheon+, reporting a raised H0. Probe-side items are complementary: an all-sky cluster catalog and the 2MASS Redshift Survey give BAO distance constraints consistent with DESI DR2, and a proposed Rubin twilight program for nearby Type Ia supernovae improves the dark-energy figure of merit in simulations. The decihertz eccentric IMRI paper concerns gravitational-wave template bias and is outside this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
